---
/**
 * /supply-chain/ — the manufacturer door. Published 2026-09-11 as a page selling
 * three audits with the seven demos shown underneath as proof; rebuilt 2026-09-20
 * as the page that SELLS the seven factory tools (D118, Phase 6).
 *
 * D29 DEFERRED THIS IN ITS OWN WORDS — "secondary, or a later venture as the
 * practice grows" — and D118 ended the deferral outright: the manufacturer is one
 * of the three doors on the home page, and this is what is behind it.
 *
 * THE TOOLS ARE THE PRODUCT, AND AN AUDIT IS A TOOL RUN ONCE. The operator
 * reversed the old shape on 2026-09-20: each tool is built to order for one plant
 * on its own extract, or run once for the written answer it produces, and the two
 * audits that remain each name the tool behind them. The change-order cutover
 * audit left because no tool stands behind it, and an audit with no tool behind
 * it is a day of hand work sold as a product.
 *
 * THE FLOOR PER PLANT IS PUBLISHED (Phase 7 of D118), from src/lib/pricing.js
 * through `industrialPrice`, with its fourth-product test written beside the
 * constant and a render counter in check-dist.mjs. It is painted once here, in
 * the terms panel, beside its qualifier; a hand-typed copy anywhere is what
 * `npm run gate` refuses.
 *
 * FIXED PRICE PER PLANT, NEVER A DAY RATE, AND THE REASON IS ARITHMETIC. Day-rate
 * work in this field is weekday-business-hours work, and src/lib/consult-hours.js
 * publishes weekday evenings and weekend mornings — none of it inside a business
 * day. A day rate would be selling hours that do not exist, and the page says so
 * to the reader rather than only to the next editor.
 *
 * THE EMPLOYER IS NEVER NAMED AND NEITHER IS ANY PLANT. D1 and D8 hold without
 * exception. scripts/verify-industrial.mjs reads this page's RENDERED text for
 * stray plant codes since Phase 6, with P10 planted into <main> as its control —
 * the sentence here claimed that before it was true, and the gate only opened
 * /work/<slug>/. So no string on this page or in `supplyChain` carries a bare
 * four-digit number.
 *
 * THE LIST IS DERIVED, NEVER TYPED (D22). The tools are read out of workGroups by
 * band, the same filter /work/ and /llms.txt use, so a group joining the scale
 * band joins this page for free.
 *
 * NO PAY BUTTON AND NO BOOKING LINK. This starts with somebody describing a number
 * they do not trust, which is a conversation rather than a checkout.
 */
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { supplyChain, industrialPrice } from '../data/services';
import { countWord } from '../lib/count-words.js';
import { priorTradeCountWord } from '../lib/trades.js';
import { workGroups, demos } from '../data/demos';
import { Boxes, Ruler, ArrowUpRight } from '@lucide/astro';

const origin = new URL(Astro.site!).origin;

/* DERIVED, NEVER TYPED — the same filter /work/index.astro and /llms.txt.ts use. */
const scaleGroups = workGroups.filter((g) => g.band === 'scale');
const scaleCount = scaleGroups.reduce((n, g) => n + g.slugs.length, 0);
const bySlug = new Map(demos.map((d) => [d.slug, d]));

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Service',
    '@id': `${origin}/supply-chain/#service`,
    name: 'Factory planning tools for manufacturers, built to order per plant',
    serviceType: 'Supply chain software',
    provider: { '@id': `${origin}/#business` },
    description:
      'Planning, inbound and master-data tools built to order for one plant on its own extract, or run once for the written answer. Quoted per plant, agreed before anything starts.',
  },
];
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Numbers your planning system is sure about"
  description="Factory planning tools for manufacturers, built to order for one plant on its own extract or run once for the answer. Open each one first, on invented data; quoted per plant."
  schema={schema}
>
  {/* ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The widest measure on the page for the claim, and the same shape D113
      gave every hero on the site. What follows walks content, popout, popout
      for the column and surface, canvas, deep for the ground, with the rhythm
      tightening under the run-once band — no two neighbors share more than one
      heavy signal, and the palette does none of the work. */}
  <Section width="feature" class="border-b border-line">
    <Fragment slot="backdrop">
      <div class="bg-grid bg-grid-fade pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-60"></div>
    </Fragment>
      <p class="mono-label">For manufacturers · built to order per plant · never a day rate</p>
      <h1 class="statement mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        The numbers your planning system is sure about.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        {supplyChain.whoItIsFor}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        I have spent the last few years on a planning floor, and before that in operations in {priorTradeCountWord()}
        other industries. The tools below are the work I do on a weekday: not advice about it.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        {/* `btn` CARRIES THE SHAPE AND `btn-primary` ONLY THE PAINT — the
            strongest call to action on this page once shipped without the
            first of them and painted a hard-edged rectangle. Same defect, same
            repair, as /quoted/ on 2026-09-13. `quote` is the intent because a
            manufacturer arriving here is pricing work. */}
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?intent=quote">
          Tell me which number you do not trust <ArrowUpRight class="size-4" />
        </a>
        <a class="link-sweep text-sm" href="#tools">Or open one first →</a>
      </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ── The tools, which are the product ────────────────────────────────────
      The surface ground and the reading column against the hero's canvas and
      widest measure. The count derives; the cards read the same fields /work/
      renders, so a tool cannot look like two products on two pages. */}
  <Section id="tools" tone="surface" width="content">
      <p class="mono-label">What you can buy</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        {countWord(scaleCount, { capital: true })} factory tools, each built to order.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{supplyChain.own}</p>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Each runs here on invented data from a fictional manufacturer, with nothing to install and no
        account to make. Open it first; the arithmetic in it is the arithmetic that would run on yours.
      </p>

      {scaleGroups.map((g) => (
        <div class="mt-9">
          <p class="mono-label text-cyan-deep">{g.label}</p>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
            {g.slugs.map((slug) => {
              const d = bySlug.get(slug);
              return d ? (
                <a href={`/work/${slug}/`} class="panel lift flex flex-col gap-2 p-5">
                  <h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink">{d.name}</h3>
                  <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{d.blurb}</p>
                  <span class="link-sweep mt-1 text-sm">Open it →</span>
                </a>
              ) : null;
            })}
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
  </Section>

  {/* ── Or run once ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Back to canvas and in to the reading column, tight under the grid. Each
      audit names the tool behind it, because an audit with no tool behind it is
      the shape D118 cut. */}
  <Section width="popout" density="tight">
      <p class="mono-label">Or run once</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        The answer, without the tool.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{supplyChain.once}</p>

      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {supplyChain.audits.map((a) => {
          const tool = bySlug.get(a.slug);
          return (
            <div class="panel flex flex-col gap-3 p-6">
              <span class="grid h-11 w-11 place-items-center rounded-lg border border-line bg-canvas text-accent-2">
                <Ruler size={20} aria-hidden="true" />
              </span>
              <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{a.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{a.body}</p>
              {tool && (
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-faint">
                  The tool behind it: <a href={`/work/${a.slug}/`} class="link-sweep text-ink-muted">{tool.name}</a>
                </p>
              )}
            </div>
          );
        })}
      </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ── How it is sold, and the refusal ─────────────────────────────────────
      THE DEEP GROUND IS SPENT HERE ON PURPOSE, and it is the heaviest signal
      this page has. This is the only band that states terms rather than
      offering something — the fixed price per plant, the reason there is no
      day rate, and the refusal to take this work from appliance manufacturers
      — so the page stopping is what the ground should say. `deep` and not
      `instrument`: both panels are sized for a light ground. Phase 7 puts the
      floor and its qualifier into the first panel, in one box. */}
  <Section tone="deep" width="popout">
    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="panel flex flex-col gap-3 p-7">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Boxes class="size-5 text-accent" />
          <span class="mono-label">How it is priced</span>
        </div>
        {/* THE FIGURE AND ITS QUALIFIER IN ONE BOX (Phase 7 of D118), and
            verify-industrial.mjs requires them painted within 400 characters
            of each other here, for the reason verify-website.mjs states. */}
        <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">{industrialPrice.line}</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{industrialPrice.qualifier}</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{supplyChain.howItIsSold}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel flex flex-col gap-3 p-7">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Ruler class="size-5 text-secondary" />
          <span class="mono-label">What is never sold</span>
        </div>
        <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">
          Nothing built before it is bought.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
          No tool here is built speculatively for a plant that has not asked for it, no license is
          sold, and the demo you can open is the demo: yours runs on your extract and nobody else's.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">{supplyChain.conflictRule}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</MarketingLayout>
